    "result_text": "All 281 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-normalization behavior in the owner-creation endpoint.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\nBefore computing the customer code, the owner's city is now resolved via a new `resolveCityName` helper:\n- If any existing owner already lives in that city (compared case-insensitively), the new owner adopts that owner's **exact existing spelling** \u2014 keeping a city's spelling canonical.\n- Otherwise the supplied city is **title-cased** (each whitespace-separated word capitalized, remaining letters lower-cased) via `toTitleCase`.\n\nThe resolved city is what gets stored and returned in the `city` field. Because `customerCode` derives from `city.toUpperCase(...)`, the existing customer-code logic is unaffected.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`:\n- `createOwnerTitleCasesCity` \u2014 posts a brand-new city with mixed casing (`\"nORth \u2026\"`) and asserts it's returned title-cased.\n- `createOwnerReusesExistingCitySpelling` \u2014 seeds an owner with an odd spelling (`\"gOtHaM\u2026\"`), posts a new owner with a different casing of the same city, and asserts the response reuses the seeded exact spelling.\n\nFull suite: **281 tests, 0 failures**.",
